    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA15:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "When David had come to the top, where God was worshiped, behold, Hushai the Archite came to meet him with his tunic torn and earth on his head."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA15:37",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Hushai, David’s friend, came into the city; and Absalom came into Jerusalem."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Hushai the Archite, David’s friend, had come to Absalom, Hushai said to Absalom, “Long live the king! Long live the king!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Absalom said to Hushai, “Is this your kindness to your friend? Why didn’t you go with your friend?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA16:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hushai said to Absalom, “No; but whomever the LORD and this people and all the men of Israel have chosen, I will be his, and I will stay with him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:5",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Absalom said, “Now call Hushai the Archite also, and let’s hear likewise what he says.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Hushai had come to Absalom, Absalom spoke to him, saying, “Ahithophel has spoken like this. Shall we do what he says? If not, speak up.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hushai said to Absalom, “The counsel that Ahithophel has given this time is not good.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Hushai said moreover, “You know your father and his men, that they are mighty men, and they are fierce in their minds, like a bear robbed of her cubs in the field. Your father is a man of war, and will not lodge with the people."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Absalom and all the men of Israel said, “The counsel of Hushai the Archite is better than the counsel of Ahithophel.” For the LORD had ordained to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel, to the intent that the LORD might bring evil on Absalom."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA17:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Hushai said to Zadok and to Abiathar the priests, “Ahithophel counseled Absalom and the elders of Israel that way; and I have counseled this way."
      }
    ],
